The terminal UI, supertag-tui, embeds OpenTUI's native library (libopentui, from the
@opentui/core-PLATFORM 0.9.4 packages, https://github.com/anomalyco/opentui at tag v0.9.4; MIT).
That library statically links a decode-only build of FFmpeg 9.0.2 (https://ffmpeg.org), licensed
under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later, and zlib. OpenTUI's package
also carries the licenses of the other components it names (Ghostty, Yoga, libwebp, lcms2, stb,
wuffs, gdtoa, Zig, LLVM, and others). Those licenses, and FFMPEG-SOURCE.md, which names the exact
FFmpeg source and its SHA-256, are in licenses/opentui/ of the release archive.

The exact FFmpeg source that library was built from, ffmpeg-9.0.2.tar.xz, is attached to the same
GitHub release as this archive (https://github.com/atemaguer/supertag/releases), and listed in
that release's SHA256SUMS; it is also at https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-9.0.2.tar.xz. OpenTUI's
source at tag v0.9.4 holds the build configuration, packages/native/scripts/build-ffmpeg.ts, and
the build scripts that rebuild and relink libopentui with a modified FFmpeg. supertag-tui loads a
replacement library from the file that OPENTUI_LIB_PATH names.

The desktop app bundles two typefaces, each under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1: Geist
(Copyright 2024 The Geist Project Authors, https://github.com/vercel/geist-font) and Bricolage
Grotesque (Copyright 2022 The Bricolage Grotesque Project Authors,
https://github.com/ateliertriay/bricolage), both from their Fontsource packages
(@fontsource-variable/geist and @fontsource-variable/bricolage-grotesque, 5.3.0). Their licenses
are in Resources/licenses/ of the app.
